INTERPRETATION (honest, bounded to what was actually measured):

- All 4 turns completed successfully with real, coherent, on-topic
  content (a genuine bug-review -> fix -> test -> commit-message
  sequence), growing conversation context each turn (1477 -> 3980
  chars) exactly as a real multi-turn session would.
- Per-turn latency: 0.59s - 4.88s. Total 4-turn wall-clock: 13.0s.
- tok/s stayed CONSISTENT across all 4 turns (57.3 - 61.8 tok/s) with
  NO progressive degradation - this is the direct, measured contrast
  to section 10m's documented CPU-only finding of speed degrading from
  ~11.75 tok/s down to ~2.9-3.0 tok/s over 4 turns, which is what
  caused the client's own ~180s idle timeout (and even a patient 900s
  outer budget) to repeatedly fire before a turn could finish.
- 13.0s total for 4 full turns is comfortably within BOTH previously-
  documented client-side budgets (the ~180s per-request idle timeout
  and the 900s patient internal budget) by roughly one to two orders
  of magnitude of headroom - a real, measured, large margin, not a
  narrow pass.

